WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:04.060
The anterior epithelium, here, which will become a

2
00:00:04.100 --> 00:00:06.710
part, here, which is called the cornea,

3
00:00:06.750 --> 00:00:07.730
there, you see,

4
00:00:10.780 --> 00:00:13.520
l epithelium, which is therefore a mesenchymal

5
00:00:13.560 --> 00:00:14.040
tissue,

6
00:00:18.020 --> 00:00:19.890
whereas the conjunctival tissue,

7
00:00:19.930 --> 00:00:21.910
we could say it is an epithelial,

8
00:00:21.950 --> 00:00:23.500
thus a limiting tissue.

9
00:00:29.190 --> 00:00:32.050
Then we have what is called the anterior chamber,

10
00:00:32.090 --> 00:00:33.460
the pupillary orifice.

11
00:00:36.950 --> 00:00:39.740
You have three major tunics that surround the eye.

12
00:00:42.690 --> 00:00:44.650
So it's as if they were three socks,

13
00:00:44.690 --> 00:00:45.890
one inside the other.

14
00:00:46.990 --> 00:00:49.060
The first sock is called the sclera.

15
00:00:51.410 --> 00:00:53.970
It is continuous with the cornea anteriorly.

16
00:00:56.141 --> 00:00:58.491
transparent, then you have the limbus,

17
00:00:58.531 --> 00:00:59.791
then the white part.

18
00:01:00.561 --> 00:01:02.041
This is the first layer.

19
00:01:02.081 --> 00:01:04.201
I remove this first sock, and then,

20
00:01:04.241 --> 00:01:07.551
we encounter an important layer called the choroid.

21
00:01:08.721 --> 00:01:11.131
And the choroid, we see here, you see,

22
00:01:11.171 --> 00:01:13.821
which is a layer that is extremely vascularized.

23
00:01:15.761 --> 00:01:18.141
And this choroid continues anteriorly,

24
00:01:18.181 --> 00:01:19.741
here, with what is called

25
00:01:22.361 --> 00:01:22.961
the iris.

26
00:01:24.212 --> 00:01:27.482
Iridology is a reading of the mesodermal vascular

27
00:01:27.522 --> 00:01:27.872
system.

28
00:01:31.492 --> 00:01:34.412
By observing the eye, you can see information about

29
00:01:34.452 --> 00:01:36.702
trophic changes of a vascular nature.

30
00:01:38.352 --> 00:01:41.482
This is expressed in the iris, which are sensors

31
00:01:41.522 --> 00:01:43.592
where they can store, for example,

32
00:01:44.432 --> 00:01:44.552
of sulfur.

33
00:01:45.272 --> 00:01:46.902
We can store a lot of things.

34
00:01:47.512 --> 00:01:48.932
And we can learn to read.

35
00:01:48.972 --> 00:01:51.372
There is a mapping of how it will be arranged.

36
00:01:52.282 --> 00:01:54.462
there will be another relationship that will be

37
00:01:54.502 --> 00:01:56.682
important, which is the ciliary processes and then

38
00:01:56.722 --> 00:01:59.262
there will be a relationship with what we call the

39
00:01:59.302 --> 00:01:59.789
suspensory

40
00:02:00.542 --> 00:02:02.792
muscles of the iris, which we will see in detail

41
00:02:02.832 --> 00:02:04.870
later to understand their physiology.

42
00:02:05.842 --> 00:02:07.702
So we see the crystalline lens,

43
00:02:09.142 --> 00:02:11.172
the different chambers that will appear,

44
00:02:11.212 --> 00:02:12.502
the pupillary orifice,

45
00:02:14.202 --> 00:02:15.545
Here, a little further,

46
00:02:16.402 --> 00:02:18.642
in this choroid with the iris, you see.

47
00:02:20.353 --> 00:02:22.503
which will form an important link with what is

48
00:02:22.543 --> 00:02:24.213
called the suspensory ligament.

49
00:02:27.093 --> 00:02:29.013
There is also a ciliary muscle; there is an

50
00:02:29.053 --> 00:02:31.273
accommodation system that will occur.

51
00:02:33.173 --> 00:02:36.373
Well, this accommodation system involves this lens,

52
00:02:36.413 --> 00:02:38.313
which we call the crystalline lens,

53
00:02:38.353 --> 00:02:41.073
by the ciliary muscles, with the ora serrata;

54
00:02:41.113 --> 00:02:42.743
well, we'll see that later,

55
00:02:44.273 --> 00:02:45.903
which will increase, change the shape

56
00:02:48.424 --> 00:02:51.664
of my lens slightly, to allow the image to integrate

57
00:02:51.704 --> 00:02:53.414
correctly on the retinal plane.

58
00:02:56.344 --> 00:02:57.994
First layer, the sclera.

59
00:02:59.884 --> 00:03:01.704
Second layer, the choroid.

60
00:03:02.784 --> 00:03:04.454
Third layer, the retina.

61
00:03:06.744 --> 00:03:08.864
The nervous tissue, the deepest,

62
00:03:08.904 --> 00:03:11.324
which is truly the expression of the brain.

63
00:03:11.684 --> 00:03:14.394
With the colobomatous cleft, which gives rise to the

64
00:03:14.434 --> 00:03:15.064
anomaly.

65
00:03:16.495 --> 00:03:19.435
for the hyaloid artery and vessels which will form

66
00:03:19.475 --> 00:03:21.015
the retinal vessels, etc.

67
00:03:24.695 --> 00:03:27.605
Colobomatous cleft, do you understand what it was?

68
00:03:27.775 --> 00:03:30.025
With, you see, this remnant here,

69
00:03:30.065 --> 00:03:31.875
then this closure that will occur.

70
00:03:32.755 --> 00:03:35.845
So the retina, in fact, is the innermost layer of

71
00:03:35.885 --> 00:03:36.425
